{"id":"word:hebrew:H5158","type":"word","title":"נַחַל","subtitle":"H5158 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a stream , especially a winter torrent ; (by implication) a (narrow) valley (in which a brook runs); also a shaft (of a mine)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נַחַל (H5158) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 141 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נַחַל (nachal) means a stream , especially a winter torrent ; (by implication) a (narrow) valley (in which a brook runs); also a shaft (of a mine) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 32."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נַחַל","transliteration":"nachal","pronunciation":"nakh'-al","strong":"H5158","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5158","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["נַ֣חַל","נַ֥חַל","נַ֨חַל","בְּ/נַ֣חַל","הַ/נַּ֔חַל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",39],["HTd/Ncmsa",22],["HR/Ncmsc",17],["HRd/Ncmsa",11],["HNcmsa",11],["HNcmpc",6],["HTd/Ncmpa",4],["HR/Ncmsa",4],["HNcmpa",4],["HR/Ncmpc",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"a stream , especially a winter torrent ; (by implication) a (narrow) valley (in which a brook runs); also a shaft (of a mine)","usage":"brook, flood, river, stream, valley.","full":"H5158. nachal I. נַ֫חַל noun masculine 2Kin 3:16 torrent, torrent-valley, wady (Ecclus 40:13; 40:16; Late Hebrew id., stream (rare); נַחְלָא ᵑ7 , = Biblical Hebrew; Assyrian na—lu = Biblical Hebrew; Lag BN 140 Anm. thinks Νεῖλος may be from Νεέλ = נַחַל pronounced * נִהִל ; on ׳נ in Sabean proper name, of a location, see Hal Rev. Sémit. Iv (1896), 80, 1, 14 ); — absolute ׳נ Gen 32:24 +, נַ֫חְלָה Psa 124:4 ; construct נַחַל Gen 26:17 +; with ה locative, 34:5 so read also Ezek 47:19 ; 48:28 (where נַחֲלָ֫ה ᵑ0 ; see Thes); dual נַחֲלַיִם 47:9 , but read ᵐ5 הַנַּחַל . ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵑ7 Co Berthol; plural נְחָלִים Num 21:4 +; נַחֲלֵי Deut 8:7 +; suffix נְחֶלֶיהָ Isa 34:9 ; &#8212; 1 torrent , of rushing water in narrow channel Judg 5:21 (3 t. in verse); 4:7 , 13 ; Psa 83:10 (all of קִישֹׁן , q. v.); mountain torrent Deut 9:21 (compare Exod 32:20 ); so Amos 5:24 (simile of righteousness); ׳הַנּ הַשּׁוֺטֵף 2Chr 32:4 (|| מַעְיָנוֺת ); נ ׳נֶהְמְּכוּ לְזֶפֶת Isa 34:9 ; simile of tears Lam 2:18 ; hyperb. שָֿׁ֑מֶן׳נ Micah 6:7 torrents of oil , compare of honey and curd Job 20:17 (|| נְהָרִים מְּלַגּוֺת, ); figurative ׳נ בְלִיַּעַל 2Sam 22:5 torrents of worthlessness (|| מָ֫וֶת מִשְׁבְּרֵי ), = Psa 18:5 ; ׳נ שׁוֺטֵף simile of glory of nations Isa 66:12 , figurative of invaders Jer 47:2 (|| מַיִס ), or foes Psa 124:4 ( נַ֫חְלָה , see above); 1Kin 17:4 , 6 (for drinking), drying up in summer 17:7 ( יָבֵשׁ ; all of Elijah's stream כְּרִית , q. v.); for drinking also Psa 110:7 , and (figurative) ׳נ עֲדָנֶיךָ 36:9 ; Job 6:15 (twice in verse) ( נְחָלִים אֲפִיק ; in simile); of water bursting from rock Psa 78:20 ( שָׁטַף , || מַיִם ), compare 74:15 (+ מַעְיָן ); figurative of חָכְמָה מְקוֺר Prov 18:4 ( ׳נ נֹבֵּעַ ; || עֲמֻקִים מַיִם ); more Generally = stream, brook, river (chiefly late) Isa 11:15 (divisions of river, נָהָר ) in desert 35:6 (|| מַיִם ), Jer 31:9 ( מַיִם נַחֲלֵי ), Ezek 47:5 (twice in verse); 47:9 b (all strike out Co), 47:6 ; 47:7 ; 47:9 a (read הַנַּחַל , see above), 47:12 ; containing fish, etc. Lev 11:9-10 , (|| יַמִּים מַיִם, ), Eccl 1:7 (twice in verse); figurative י ׳רוּחַ , Isa 30:28 ( ׳נ שׁוֺטֵף , 30:33 ( ׳נ גָּפְרִית ). 2 Torrent-valley, wady , as stream-bed 1Sam 17:40 ; Neh 2:15 ; Isa 57:6 ; with torrent flowing through it, ׳נ אֵיתָן Deut 21:4 (twice in verse); 21:6 , מַיִם נַחֲלֵי אֶרֶץ 8:7 (|| בַּבִּקְעָה יֹּצְאִים וּתְהֹמֹת עֲיָנֹת ), compare 10:7 , 1Kin 18:5 (|| הַמַיִם מַעְיְנֵי ), Psa 104:10 ; abode of Elijah 1Kin 17:3 , 5 (compare 17:4 ; 17:6 ; 17:7 above); נ ׳עֹרְבֵי Prov 30:17 (compare 1Kin 17:4 , 6 ); ׳נ הַבַּתּוֺת Isa 7:19 as home of bees; fertile, ׳נ אֶשְׁכֹּל Num 13:23-24 , (E); הַנּ ׳אִבֵּי Song 6:11 ; ׳עַרְבֵינֿ poplars of the wady Lev 23:40 (H), Job 40:22 ; ׳נ עֲרָבִים Isa 15:7 ; needing water Gen 26:17 ( ׳נ גְּרָר ), 26:19 (J), compare 2Kin 3:16-17 , place for refuse, ruins, etc. 2Sam 17:13 ; in poetry also as wild, remote ravine Job 30:6 , compare הַנְּחָלִים בְּצוּר 22:24 ; place of child-sacrifice Isa 57:5 ; burial-place Job 21:33 ( נ ׳רִגְבֵי ), — Num 24:6 see II. נַ֫חַל . Particular wadys designate localities: אַרְנוֺן Num 21:14 (E), Deut 2:24 , 36 (twice in verse); 3:8 , 12 , 16 (twice in verse); 4:48 ; Josh 12:1-2 ,(twice in verse); 13:9 (twice in verse) (all D), 13:16 ; 13:16 (P), 2Kin 10:33 ; אֶשְׁכֹּל Num 32:9 (J), Deut 1:24 בְּשׂוֺר 1Sam 30:9-10 , 21 ; גָּד 2Sam 24:5 ; זֶרֶד Num 21:12 (E), Deut 2:13 (twice in verse); 2:14 ; יַכֹּק Gen 32:24 (J), Deut 2:37 ; 3:16 ; Josh 12:2 (all D); קִדְרוֺן 2Sam 15:23 ; 1Kin 2:37 ; 15:13 ; 18:40 ; 1Ki 23:6 (twice in verse); 2Sam 23:12 ; 2Chr 15:16 ; 29:16 ; 30:14 ; Jer 31:40 ; קָנָה Josh 16:8 ; 17:9 (3 t. in verse) (all P); שׂוֺרֵק Judg 16:4 ; ׳נ הַשִּׁטִּים Joel 4:18; מִצְרַיִם ׳נ is southwest limit of Palestine (Assyrian na—al [ mat ] Muƒri , Dl Par. 310 Schr COT Num 34:5 ) 34:5 (P), Josh 15:4 (D), 15:47 (P), 1Kin 8:65 ; 2Kin 24:7 , 2 ; Chron 7:8 ; Isa 27:12 , + (omit מצרים ) Ezek 47:19 ; 48:28 (see above); so read also possibly Amos 6:14 (see עֲרָבָה : usually identified with Wâdy el-Arîsh ; on Wkl's different view, see references below מִצְרַיִם near the end); on identification of ׳נ Josh 15:7 ; 19:11 (both P), 2Sam 23:30 = 1Chr 11:32 ; 2Chr 20:16 ; 33:14 , see Commentaries; הַנְּחָלִים אָשֶׁד Num 21:15 , see אֶשֶׁד . 3 Miner's shaft , נ ׳מָּרַץ Job 28:4 . II. [ נַ֫חַל ] noun [masculine] perhaps palm-tree (Arabic , noun of individual meaning ; see Perles JQ, July, 1899, 688 ); — only plural absolute, נִטָּ֑יוּ כִּנְחָלִים Num 24:6 like palm-trees, which are stretched out, spread out (as to foliage). So Perles l.c , who compares נחל כערבי Ecclus 50:12e, ᵐ5 ὡς στελέχη φοινικων .","rootNote":"or (feminine) נַחְלָה ; (Psalm 124:4), or נַחֲלָה ; (Ezekiel 47:19; Ezekiel 48:28), from 5157 in its original sense;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 32","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 32","1Kgs 2 37","1Kgs 8 65","1Kgs 15 13","1Kgs 17 3","1Kgs 17 4","1Kgs 17 5","1Kgs 17 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":141,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 32","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִ/נַּ֣חֲלֵי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmpc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 37","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":37,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 65","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":65,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 15 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":15,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/נַ֥חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 3","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/נַ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 4","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵ/הַ/נַּ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 5","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/נַ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נַּ֖חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 7","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּ֑חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 5","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נְּחָלִ֑ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 40","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַ֣חַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 15 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":15,"verse":5